    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L04-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "4.3: Got Caffeine?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Imagine a medicine has a half-life of 3 hours. If a patient takes 200 mg of the medicine, then the amount of medicine in their body, in mg, can be modeled by the function \\(\\displaystyle f(t) = 200 \\boldcdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^t\\).…",
